&= \frac{14}{\sqrt{3}}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{3}}=\boxed{\frac{14\sqrt{3}}{3}} \text{ cm}.
\end{align*}[asy]
unitsize(0.3 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, P, U, V, W, X, Y, Z;

A = 14*sqrt(3)/3*dir(60);
B = 14*sqrt(3)/3*dir(120);
C = 14*sqrt(3)/3*dir(180);
D = 14*sqrt(3)/3*dir(240);
E = 14*sqrt(3)/3*dir(300);
F = 14*sqrt(3)/3*dir(360);
P = extension(A + (0,-4), B + (0,-4), A + 5*dir(210), F + 5*dir(210));

U = (P + reflect(A,B)*(P))/2;
V = (P + reflect(B,C)*(P))/2;
W = (P + reflect(C,D)*(P))/2;
X = (P + reflect(D,E)*(P))/2;
Y = (P + reflect(E,F)*(P))/2;
Z = (P + reflect(F,A)*(P))/2;

draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--cycle);
draw(U--X,dotted);
draw(V--Y,dotted);
draw(W--Z,dotted);
draw(A--P);
draw(B--P);
draw(C--P);
draw(D--P);
draw(E--P);
draw(F--P);

label("$A$", A, dir(60));
label("$B$", B, dir(120));
label("$C$", C, dir(180));
label("$D$", D, dir(240));
label("$E$", E, dir(300));
label("$F$", F, dir(360));
label("$P$", P, SW, UnFill);
label("$4$", (P + U)/2, dir(180));
label("$6$", (P + V)/2, SW);
label("$9$", (P + W)/2, SE);
label("$10$", (P + X)/2, dir(180));
label("$8$", (P + Y)/2, SW);
label("$5$", (P + Z)/2, SE);
[/asy]

By the sum of cubes factorization, \[z^9 - 1 = (z^6+z^3+1)(z^3-1).\]The roots of $z^9 - 1$ are the nine $9^{\text{th}}$ roots of unity, and the roots of $z^3 - 1$ are the three $3^{\text{th}}$ roots of unity. It follows that the roots of $z^6 + z^3 + 1$ are the six other roots of $z^9 - 1$: that is, the six $9^{\text{th}}$ roots of unity which are not $3^{\text{rd}}$ roots of unity.

The arguments of the ninth roots of unity in the complex plane are $0^\circ, 40^\circ, 80^\circ, \dots, 320^\circ.$

